dst, and saith unto them, Peace be unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzAnd when he had so said, he shewed unto them his hands and his side. Then were the disciples glad, when they saw the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Then said Jesus to them again, Peace be unto you: as my Father hath sent me, even so send I you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And when he had said this, he breathed on them, and saith unto them, Receive ye the Holy Ghost:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlwhose soever sins ye remit, they are remitted unto them; and whose soever sins ye retain, they are retained.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQBut Thomas, one of the twelve, called Didymus, was not with them when Jesus came.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ÷The other disciples therefore said unto him, We have seen the Lord. But he said unto them, Except I shall see in his hands the print of the nails, and put my finger into the print of the nails, and thrust my hand into his side, I will not believe.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And after eight days again his disciples were within, and Thomas with them: then came Jesus, the doors being shut, and stood in the midst, and said, Peace be unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢Then saith he to Thomas, Reach hither thy finger, and behold my hands; and reach hither thy hand, and thrust it into my side: and be not faithless, but believing.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:And Thomas answered and said unto him, My Lord and my God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆJesus saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd many other signs truly did Jesus in the presence of his disciples, which are not written in this book:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbut these are written, that ye might believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God; and that believing ye might have life through his name.¦layout ªlast_verse